## 7. Root Cause and Remediation

| Issue | Root cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| SSRF in `preview.php` | User input used directly as a fetch target, filtered only by a substring blocklist | Allowlist expected domains/schemes; never let user input reach an outbound request directly |
| Internal port scan / gopher tunnel | SSRF had no network-level containment — the web server itself could reach internal-only ports | Network segmentation: the app server should not be able to route to internal management ports at all |
| CVE-2025-29927 | Next.js trusted a client-settable header (`x-middleware-subrequest`) as proof of an internal-only call | Patch to a fixed Next.js version; never let internal control-flow signals be set by untrusted input |
| 2FA bypass via cookie | 2FA completion state stored client-side and trusted as-is, with no signature/integrity check | Store session/auth state server-side (or sign and verify it, e.g. with an HMAC) so the client can't forge it |

